---
import Icon from './SideworkIcon.astro';
---
<section class="sw-panel sw-agents" id="agents" aria-labelledby="agents-title" hidden>
  <div class="sw-composer-heading"><div><h2 id="agents-title">Tell your project’s story</h2><p>Work with your agent to explain what you built, why, and what you learned.</p></div><a class="sw-button" href="https://github.com/mager/sidework/tree/main/plugins/sidework">Install guide <Icon name="external" size={16}/></a></div>
  <div class="sw-agent-task"><p class="sw-agent-intro" id="agent-story-task">Help me tell the story of what I built for Sidework. Use the current repository’s public README, source, and demo as evidence. Ask me about my motivation and learning, and check what I personally built. Leave unknown claims blank. Prepare one project with a review link and JSON file if Sidework MCP is connected; otherwise give me a repository import link and the story to review. I will review and explicitly save in Sidework. Publishing is a separate browser action.</p><button type="button" class="sw-button sw-primary" id="copy-agent-story">Copy story task</button></div>
  <p class="sw-agent-purpose">Paste this into your agent while working in a project, or add a public repository URL. The Sidework plugin helps with source evidence; the optional MCP connection prepares a review link and file.</p>
  <ol class="sw-agent-flow" aria-label="Project story workflow"><li><strong>Draft</strong><span>Your agent reads evidence and asks for your context.</span></li><li><strong>Review</strong><span>Open the returned link or file and check the story.</span></li><li><strong>Save</strong><span>Explicitly save to your private account in Sidework. Legacy sessions save in this browser.</span></li><li><strong>Publish</strong><span>Choose one reviewed project and favorites in Showcase, then publish there.</span></li></ol>
  <p class="sw-agent-boundary">Your agent cannot read private account drafts, save changes, or publish. A review link is a private draft, ready for your review.</p>
  <p id="agent-token-status" role="status" hidden></p>
  <div class="sw-agent-copy" id="agent-copy-fallback" hidden><label for="agent-copy-text" id="agent-copy-label">Copy manually</label><textarea id="agent-copy-text" readonly rows="7" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"></textarea><button type="button" class="sw-button" id="hide-agent-copy">Hide text</button></div>
  <ol class="sw-agent-steps">
    <li><h3>Install in your agent</h3><p>Use the install guide for Claude Code, Codex, or OpenCode. For Claude Code, run these commands.</p><pre><code>/plugin marketplace add mager/sidework
/plugin install sidework@sidework</code></pre><button type="button" class="sw-button" id="copy-plugin-install">Copy install commands</button></li>
    <li><h3>Ask for a project story</h3><p>Use the task above with the plugin’s <code>sidework-story</code> skill. Your agent checks public evidence and asks about your motivation and learning. Without MCP, it returns a repository import link and a story you can copy into the editor.</p></li>
    <li><h3>Connect MCP to prepare profile drafts</h3><p>This connection is optional. Create a token, then copy the MCP config into your agent. The token lasts up to 24 hours. <a href="https://github.com/mager/sidework/blob/main/docs/agents.md">MCP setup guide</a></p><button type="button" id="create-agent-token" class="sw-button">Create agent token <Icon name="plus" size={16}/></button>
      <div id="agent-token-result" hidden><label for="agent-token">Your agent token</label><input id="agent-token" type="password" readonly autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"/><div class="sw-agent-actions"><button type="button" class="sw-button" id="copy-agent-token">Copy token</button><button type="button" class="sw-button" id="copy-agent-config">Copy MCP config</button></div><p id="agent-token-expiry"></p><p>Keep the token private. It is not stored in this browser.</p></div>
      <details><summary>MCP endpoint</summary><p>Use Streamable HTTP with a Bearer token.</p><code class="sw-agent-endpoint" id="agent-endpoint"></code></details>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
